        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6c002acc9af34e7e82ea7326f66a0926",
      "statement": "The Google OAuth credentials step is included only when `features.oauthLogin` is true and `oauthProviders` includes `google`; `client-id` and `client-secret` are resolved from `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`/`GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` only when not already configured on the service, so a re-run against a configured service needs no secrets in the environment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L161-L201",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be419255b50901ab0833cbee26885222ea4d8ed676f0952a16204288361d101a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2dc0dde01bc4546b8ae31a31beaf431",
      "statement": "The origin-allowlist step installs the `origin-allowlist` feature if missing and adds `APP_URL` to `allowed-origins` as a set union — added, never replaced — so a service reached from both localhost and a deployed app keeps both origins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L202-L228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b4732d9dfb090f8275a1768f4a839f129a664221e8368af7db007c54442d23f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_daf35775fa7847c6820de33eb3205679",
      "statement": "The consents variant (`ulabase.setup.consents.ts`) spreads the accounts steps minus `appPointsAtService`, inserts the user schema, the `/users/_meta` schema binding, the consents PATCH permission, the two JWT claims, and the 451 guards rule, then appends the imported `appPointsAtService` last so the accounts definition has one home and the app is pointed at the service only after the gate is in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L186-L320",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3047076d146c3ebc64ec765af2799aba6487bcf8ae684812b6da2c575817226:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L46-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d76352165009c45c5f1836bdc5e0d25de0ecfb5bbf33968d43c93fa21e5e10c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1bf7e3e4d9554b33b1f579fc943d7b53",
      "statement": "Document versions live in `TOS_VERSION` and `PP_VERSION` at the top of `ulabase.setup.consents.ts`; the permission's `mergeRequest` and the guards rule's condition are both derived from them, so publishing new documents means editing those two constants, re-running the consents setup so rule and permission move together (the check compares the full condition, so a bump shows up as work outstanding), and keeping the `Version ...` line in `public/terms.html` and `public/privacy.html` in step by hand.",
      "evidence": [
